    "S-duality relates a theory at strong coupling to a theory at weak coupling, letting physicists calculate in regimes perturbation theory cannot reach.",
    "Witten argued at Strings 95 that all five theories are limits of one eleven-dimensional theory, M-theory, whose low-energy limit is eleven-dimensional supergravity.",
    "Polchinski's D-branes are the objects on which open strings end, and their tension scaling as one over the coupling is what made the dualities concrete and checkable.",
